  "description": "Deterministic signed verification vector for the cross-repository trust contract. Control signs acceptance, terminalization, and terminal-arm result envelopes; runner signs execution receipts and execution-arm result envelopes. Both may carry the generic result purpose, but the envelope signer must equal the verified signer of its arm receipt. Source artifacts bind the exact git-archive-tar-v1 format, id, sha256, and byte length. The producer (interlinked-cloud, WebCrypto) and consumer (interlinked-cli, node:crypto) must reproduce these exact bytes. Contract: result_hash = sha256(canonicalJson(envelope minus seq/occurred_at/result_hash/signature)); envelope signature = Ed25519 over utf8(canonicalJson({key_id, occurred_at, result_hash})); receipt signature = Ed25519 over utf8(canonicalJson({key_id, payload})).",
